A||N||2||chrissherman||I need a 84 fiero 4cyl auto wiring diagram from the ECM to the dash||||5||
Z||000000||chrissherman||11-07-2000||07:19 PM||||Hi, From Juneau AK Help my brain is going to explode!! I need a wiring diagram from the ECM to the dash,I am up grading the 84 4cyl with a 88 4cyl out of a 88 celebrity with DIS and I know that I need the ECM from the 88 Thank's chris.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-07-2000||07:48 PM||||Is the celebrity a 2.5 or one of the aluminum motors. Either way you need allot more than the ECM. You need the whole wiring harness almost. DIS motors are not at all compatible with the distributor car's wiring harness.<P>You gain a sensor in the 2.5l DIS. Nearly All the connectors are diferant, not just at the motor but almost every other one involved as well. You can't just plug the DIS ECM into the 84 harness even if the connectors fit. 84's not wired right.<P>The best thing for putting a 2.5 cast iron DIS motor in an older car is contact <A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com/" TARGET=_blank>Kick Hill Farm</A> and get the whole harness for an 87 or 88. Doing this will solve a number of problems besides hooking up the motor. (You could connect the old headlight motors to the new harness but you should consider upgrading to the new style motors. They are allot more rugged.)<P>Assuming the celebrity motor is a 2.5 and the ECM is the same one Fiero uses, Another issue will be the PROM in the ECM. The PROM configures the VSS input of the 1227748 ECM. (The 1227748 ECM has 2 totally diferant input circuits for the VSS. They are selected thru software by a flag stored in the PROM.) You'd have to rework the whole VSS circuit to use some of the other PROMs in the Fiero.<P>Even if the celebrity is a whole differant motor and ECM the VSS will still need to be configured right or it will mess up the ECM. Some setups have a VSS feeding directly to the ECM others have a buffer circuit between the VSS and the ECM. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||11-07-2000||11:25 PM||||What specific circut(s) do you need? I also have a harness and brain out of a '87 coupe (manual trans) car if you need it. It might be in your best interest to rewire the entire rear end of the car, ie. engine, tail lights and the junction block by the battery to eliminate headaches later on. (I have it all!)||||reg||1
